<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Comp_ContaminatedFood injection for food (raw meat, prepared meals, kibble) is done in C#
       by ContagionMeatDefInjector at [StaticConstructorOnStartup], NOT via XPath here.

       Reasons XML patching is unreliable for this:
         - Raw meat defs are generated at runtime (ThingDefGenerator_Meat.ImpliedMeatDefs) and
           don't exist in the XML document at patch time at all.
         - Meals/kibble exist in XML, but an XPath patch only reaches defs that inherit from a
           specific vanilla base (MealBaseIngredientless) or match a hardcoded defName (Kibble);
           modded food defined from a different base or as a standalone def slips through.

       The C# injector detects by ingestible.foodType (Meat | Meal | Kibble), covering vanilla and
       modded food uniformly. This file is intentionally an empty patch, kept to document why. -->
</Patch>
